 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#tools-for-tracking-ai-overviews-and-where-hubspot-fits"&gt;Tools For Tracking AI Overviews And Where HubSpot Fits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#frequently-asked-questions-about-tracking-ai-overviews"&gt;Frequently Asked Questions About Tracking AI Overviews&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Why Tracking AI Overviews Matters Now&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Traditional &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/best-rank-tracker"&gt;rank-tracking tools&lt;/a&gt; cannot measure the exposure generated by AI Overviews, which now sit above featured snippets as the highest-visibility position.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AI Overviews consolidate multiple sources into a single answer, making inclusion — or exclusion — a meaningful driver of both brand perception and traffic. In my experience, this shift catches marketers off guard precisely because their rankings look fine, making the problem invisible until you know where to look.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Additional reasons for tracking matters:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Volatile citation patterns&lt;/strong&gt; — Unlike organic rankings, AI Overview citations don’t correlate reliably with ranking position. A page ranking fifth may be cited while the top result is ignored. Tracking reveals which content attributes actually earn inclusion.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Query category variation&lt;/strong&gt; — AI Overviews appear more often for informational and how-to queries than transactional ones. Knowing which target keywords trigger an overview considerably shapes your content strategy.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitive intelligence&lt;/strong&gt; — If a competitor is consistently cited for your target terms, that’s a strategic signal you can’t act on without visibility.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measurement gaps&lt;/strong&gt; — AI Overviews suppress clicks even when rankings hold, creating the “ranking fine, traffic dropping” paradox. Tracking helps explain it.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;How Tracking AI Overviews Works From Baseline To Benchmarks&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The way I think about it, tracking AI Overviews is less like checking a dashboard and more like building a case — one data point at a time. It starts with a baseline: a structured snapshot of which queries trigger AI Overviews, which cite your content, and which surface competitors. Without that starting point, there’s no meaningful way to measure change.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;From that baseline, each SERP capture adds a data point that either reinforces or challenges what you recorded before. Over weeks and months, those observations become benchmarks — reference points that reflect normal performance and allow you to distinguish meaningful shifts from routine fluctuation.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;That distinction is what separates reactive content decisions from informed ones. I’ve put together a five-step checklist below outlining how to put this into practice.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The 5-Step AI Overview Tracking Checklist&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step 1: Define your keyword set&lt;/strong&gt; — Identify informational and how-to queries most relevant to your business. Prioritize keywords where you currently rank. Transactional keywords can be deprioritized for this exercise.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step 2: Establish a baseline&lt;/strong&gt; — Run your keyword set through your tracking tool and record the initial state: which queries trigger an AI Overview, which cite your domain, and which cite competitors. This snapshot becomes your reference point.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;If you’re not sure where to start, &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/ai-search-grader"&gt;HubSpot’s AI Search Grader&lt;/a&gt; is a free, one-time diagnostic that shows how your brand currently appears in AI-generated search experiences — a useful starting point before you begin logging data over time.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step 3: Select your tracking cadence&lt;/strong&gt; — Weekly is a practical starting point; daily is appropriate for high-priority terms or during active Google update periods.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step 4: Log citations and mentions separately&lt;/strong&gt; — Record whether your content receives a citation (a linked source) or a mention (a reference without a link). Keeping the distinction between linked sources and linkless references preserves data integrity over time.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step 5: Review and act monthly&lt;/strong&gt; — Aggregate weekly data into a monthly review. Look for patterns: a lack of citations, competitors gaining ground, or content types consistently earning inclusion. Use findings to inform content updates and gap analysis.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/Pastel%20Playful%20Illustrated%20Project%20Stages%20Graphic%20Organizer%20(4).png?width=650&amp;amp;height=502&amp;amp;name=Pastel%20Playful%20Illustrated%20Project%20Stages%20Graphic%20Organizer%20(4).png" width="650" height="502" alt="Graphic displaying the 5 step AI Overview Tracking Checklist. " style="height: auto; max-width: 100%...

&lt;p&gt;If you’ve opened Claude’s Customize settings and weren’t sure whether a task called for a Skill, a connector, or a Plugin, you’re not alone.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The names sound similar, and people often use them interchangeably in casual conversation even though they do distinct jobs. This guide walks through what each one actually is, how they relate, and which one fits a given workflow, using a real example along the way instead of a hypothetical one.&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=64493837-f4dd-43b0-abee-3ef154e06092&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Connect HubSpot to Claude For Personalized Insights [Free Connector]" height="58" width="645" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/64493837-f4dd-43b0-abee-3ef154e06092.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;TL;DR:&lt;/strong&gt; Skills teach Claude a procedure, MCP connectors give it authorized access to an outside tool or data source, and Plugins package both together so a team can install everything at once.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Table of Contents&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#what-are-claude-skills-plugins-and-mcp-connectors"&gt;What are Claude skills, plugins, and MCP connectors?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-do-these-three-layers-fit-together"&gt;How do these three layers fit together?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#which-should-i-use-a-skill-plugin-or-mcp-connector"&gt;Which should I use: a skill, plugin, or MCP connector?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#what-does-a-combined-workflow-look-like"&gt;What does a combined workflow look like?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#what-are-examples-for-marketing-sales-and-service-teams"&gt;What are examples for marketing, sales, and service Teams?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#how-do-i-set-up-and-govern-these-layers"&gt;How do I set up and govern these layers?&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#frequently-asked-questions-about-claude-skills-plugins-and-mcp-connectors"&gt;Frequently Asked Questions About Claude Skills, Plugins, and MCP Connector&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#solve-with-the-right-tool"&gt;Solve with the right tool.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;What are Claude skills, plugins, and MCP connectors?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The easiest way to keep these three straight is to separate access from procedure from distribution. Each layer answers a different question.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;MCP connectors are access.&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A connector links Claude to an outside service — your files, your calendar, an issue tracker, a CRM — through a live connection called an MCP server, which the service itself runs so Claude can reach it. Once you turn a connector on, Claude can read from that service and take action in it, inside your existing permissions.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;Skills are procedure.&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A skill is a set of written instructions, sometimes with scripts and reference files attached, that Claude loads when your request matches what the skill covers. A skill teaches the how: your team’s report format, your review checklist, the brand voice you always want applied. A skill can tell Claude how to use a connector’s data, but it can’t reach a live service on its own. That’s what the connector is for.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h3&gt;Plugins are distribution.&lt;/h3&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A plugin bundles skills, MCP connectors, commands, and sub-agents into a single package that installs once and can be shared with a whole team, instead of asking every person to add each piece separately.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;If you want a broader primer on how plugins work as a category of software, &lt;a href="https://blog.hubspot.com/marketing/what-are-plugins"&gt;What are plugins?&lt;/a&gt; covers the concept outside of Claude specifically. Inside Claude’s ecosystem, a plugin can hold any mix of the pieces above, and installing it adds everything in one step.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A short glossary, since these terms get thrown around loosely:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skill&lt;/strong&gt;: written instructions Claude follows when a task matches the skill’s description.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Plugin&lt;/strong&gt;: an installable package of skills, connectors, commands, and sub-agents.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MCP (Model Context Protocol)&lt;/strong&gt;: the open protocol that lets Claude talk to outside tools and services in the first place.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MCP connector&lt;/strong&gt;: one live connection, built on MCP, between Claude and a specific service.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sub-agent&lt;/strong&gt;: a specialist Claude can delegate part of a task to; this only runs in Cowork and Claude Code, not in regular chat.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;How do these three layers fit together?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Picture a request moving through Claude in three stages: a skill can shape how Claude approaches the task, a connector lets Claude reach outside the conversation to get or change real data, and a plugin is the optional wrapper that ships a skill and a connector together as one package.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/blogbot/claude-skills-vs-plugins-vs-mcp-connectors-1-20261002-7954235.webp?width=555&amp;amp;height=684&amp;amp;name=claude-skills-vs-plugins-vs-mcp-connectors-1-20261002-7954235.webp" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 555px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;" alt="three-layer model showing Skills (procedure) → MCP connectors (access) → Plugins (distribution), paired with a simple decision tree for which one you need" width="555" height="684"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;None of the three sits “above” the others in a power ranking.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A connector without a skill still works fine, as Claude will simply use its own judgment about how to phrase requests to your CRM.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A skill without a connector also works fine — it just can’t touch live data, only whatever you paste into the conversation or whatever else Claude already has access to.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A plugin is only useful when you actually want several of these installed and shared as a unit; a single skill or a single connector doesn’t need one.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;a&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Which should I use: a skill, plugin, or MCP connector?&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Match the problem to the layer, not the other way around:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use an MCP connector when you need live access to an outside tool or data source.&lt;/strong&gt; If the task involves anything Claude can’t see just by reading the conversation — your calendar, your ticketing system, your CRM — a connector is the only layer that reaches it.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use a skill when you need a repeatable procedure, a template, or a brand voice applied consistently.&lt;/strong&gt; Anything you find yourself correcting Claude on the same way every time — a report format, a QA checklist, a tone guide — is a good candidate.&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use a plugin when you need a team-ready bundle that other people can install in one step.&lt;/strong&gt; Once you’ve got a skill and a connector that work well together, packaging them into a plugin means your team doesn’t have to hunt down and configure each piece separately.&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Combinations are common, and often t...

&lt;p&gt;Digital PR has always been about earning coverage that influences the audience you can’t reach through paid channels. While the value proposition of digital PR hasn’t changed, the definition of “showing up” has.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Get Started with HubSpot's AEO Tool" height="58" width="335" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;When buyers use answer engines to research a category, the brand that appears in those answers has earned a form of coverage that press releases and media lists weren’t designed to deliver. Earned media that appears in AI results now carries more influence than traditional coverage alone.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The PR teams pulling ahead are the ones treating AI visibility as a measurable outcome of their work — not something that happens downstream of traditional metrics.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Track which earned media placements are driving answer engine citations.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The relationship between earned media and AI visibility is real, but it’s not uniform. For example, placement in a top-tier outlet doesn’t automatically translate into a citation in an answer engine. Some publications and content types generate citations at much higher rates than others.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;If you’re measuring PR success solely by placement volume, domain authority, or estimated reach, you may be optimizing for metrics that no longer fully capture influence. The gap between traditional PR measurement and AI visibility is where accountability gets murky.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/1-Sep-28-2026-10-05-49-2196-AM.png?width=650&amp;amp;height=365&amp;amp;name=1-Sep-28-2026-10-05-49-2196-AM.png" width="650" height="365" alt="AEO for digital PR, HubSpot AEO citation analysis" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO'&lt;/a&gt;s Citation Analysis surfaces which specific publications and content categories are generating citations in answer engines. PR teams can see which third-party publications are contributing to brand visibility and which aren’t. This makes it easier to evaluate which outlets and coverage types are worth prioritizing.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;HubSpot’s marketing team recorded a 642% increase in citations for comparison articles and a 58% increase in overall mentions.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Knowing which placements are driving citations gives teams the data they need to target the publications that move their AI visibility score.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Identify and target publications that improve your AI visibility score.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Not all media outlets are created equal in answer engines. Some media outlets are cited consistently; others rarely appear. PR teams need to understand which publications influence their category because it changes media outreach, content pitching, and relationship-building priorities.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Without that data, pitching strategy defaults to reach and reputation metrics that don’t reflect AI citation patterns. The result is effort spent on outlets that don’t move the needle on AI visibility, even when the coverage is objectively good.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/AEO-for-brand-marketing-3-20260919-8343173.webp?width=567&amp;amp;height=306&amp;amp;name=AEO-for-brand-marketing-3-20260919-8343173.webp" width="567" height="306" alt="AEO for digital PR, hubspot AEO Recommendations " style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 567px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO'&lt;/a&gt;s Recommendations identify gaps in a business’s citation profile and flag the types of sources and content that are most likely to improve your brand visibility score. Teams can use those insights to build a more targeted media list and adjust their pitching strategy toward outlets with demonstrated citation influence.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Targeting the right outlets matters for AI visibility, but what ultimately counts is whether teams can connect that work to the business metrics PR is accountable for.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Measure how PR investment translates to brand visibility in AI results.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;PR reporting has always involved a mix of quantitative and qualitative measures. AEO adds a cleaner signal: changes in the AI visibility score, citations, and share of voice are directly attributable to the content and placements driving them.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Teams that connect PR activity to AI visibility outcomes can make a stronger case to stakeholders for the value of earned media.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/how%20seo%20works%2c%20example%20of%20results%20from%20hubspot%20aeo.webp?width=650&amp;amp;height=366&amp;amp;name=how%20seo%20works%2c%20example%20of%20results%20from%20hubspot%20aeo.webp" width="650" height="366" alt="AEO for digital PR, HubSpot AEO Brand Visibility Dashboard " style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO'&lt;/a&gt;s Brand Visibility Dashboard tracks brand visibility score, citations, and share of voice over time. As you run PR campaigns, you can track whether your visibility metrics shift. This gives you concrete data to connect earned media activity to AI visibility outcomes.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The publications that influence AI answers are largely the same outlets your team already builds relationships with. The difference is in knowing which placements to track, which to prioritize, and how to present the results in terms stakeholders can act on.&lt;/p&gt;  
&lt;img src="https://track.hubspot.com/__ptq.gif?a=53&amp;amp;k=14&amp;amp;r=https%3A%2F%2Fblog.hubspot.com%2Fmarketing%2Faeo-guide-for-digital-pr&amp;amp;bu=https%253A%252F%252Fblog.hubspot.com%252Fmarketing&amp;amp;bvt=rss" alt="" width="1" height="1" style="min-height:1px!important;width:1px!important;border-width:0!important;margin-top:0!important;margin-bottom:0!important;margin-right:0!important;margin-left:0!important;padding-top:0!important;padding-bottom:0!important;padding-right:0!important;padding-left:0!important; "&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Clients are asking about AEO. Some have seen competitors show up in AI results and want to know what it means. Others have read that AI is changing how buyers find vendors and want to know what their agency is doing about it.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Get Started with HubSpot's AEO Tool" height="58" width="335" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;For marketing agencies, the challenge is delivering AEO at scale. Managing visibility tracking, content optimization, and performance reporting for 10 or 20 clients — each with different products, audiences, and competitive sets — is difficult to manage manually. To turn AEO into a sustainable service, agencies need a repeatable process and the right infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Agencies that build AEO infrastructure now can make AEO part of their ongoing client services instead of treating every engagement as a one-off project.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Monitor AEO performance with one tool.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;When agencies manage AEO for a portfolio of clients, tracking each client’s brand visibility score, share of voice, and citations across multiple tools creates unnecessary work and is ultimately unsustainable.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Tool sprawl creates manual work and makes trends harder to spot. Teams end up spending time pulling data instead of using it to inform strategy. Using one tool consistently keeps benchmarking data clean.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/AEO-for-brand-marketing-2-20260919-4451880.webp?width=567&amp;amp;height=402&amp;amp;name=AEO-for-brand-marketing-2-20260919-4451880.webp" width="567" height="402" alt="AEO for marketing agencies, HubSpot AEO brand visibility " style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 567px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt;’s Brand Visibility Dashboard lets agencies track brand visibility score, citations, and share of voice in one place. Teams can monitor visibility trends, compare performance with competitors, and prioritize where to focus.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;That visibility can also connect to broader marketing outcomes. According to HubSpot internal data, AEO users generate 2.6x more leads.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The goal is to turn AEO data into a repeatable process for improving each client’s visibility. The next step is to produce the content to close the identified gaps.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Deliver AI-optimized content that earns citations for clients.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Once agencies know where a client’s visibility gaps are, the next step is creating or updating content to address them.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Getting cited in answer engines requires content that’s structured, authoritative, and aligned with the specific questions those engines are answering. That content can differ from traditional SEO, which means agencies need a way to identify the content opportunities that matter specifically for AI visibility.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Without a repeatable framework, producing citation-worthy content for multiple clients can feel like starting from scratch for every engagement. But with the right tooling in place, it becomes much easier to see which content changes are most likely to move the needle on visibility.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/AEO-for-brand-marketing-3-20260919-8343173.webp?width=567&amp;amp;height=306&amp;amp;name=AEO-for-brand-marketing-3-20260919-8343173.webp" width="567" height="306" alt="HubSpot AEO Recommendations" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 567px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt; generates Recommendations tied to a client’s current visibility gaps and brand visibility score. Agencies can use those recommendations to brief writers, prioritize edits on existing pages, and build a content roadmap that directly targets visibility improvements. That gives teams a clearer connection between what they’re seeing in AI results and the content work they recommend to clients.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;But creating and optimizing content is only part of the service. Agencies also need a simple way to show clients what changed.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Report on AEO impact and brand visibility across your client portfolio.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Clients want to see progress. An AEO report gives agencies a concrete way to show it, whether that is citation counts, share of voice trends, and brand visibility score movement over time. These metrics turn an abstract concept into something agencies can bring to a monthly review meeting along with other marketing performance data.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The problem is that building those reports manually doesn’t scale. Pulling data from different sources for every account takes time and can lead to inconsistent reporting from one client to the next.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/how%20seo%20works%2c%20example%20of%20results%20from%20hubspot%20aeo.webp?width=650&amp;amp;height=366&amp;amp;name=how%20seo%20works%2c%20example%20of%20results%20from%20hubspot%20aeo.webp" width="650" height="366" alt=" aeo for marketing agencies, brand visibility dashboard" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt;’s Brand Visibility Dashboard gives marketing agencies exportable visibility data that agencies can use in client-facing reports. They can track changes over time and tie visibility improvements back to the content and outreach work they are doing. That makes reporting part of the AEO workflow instead of another manual task at the end of the month.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Systemize AEO for all your clients.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;For agencies, scaling AEO is less about adding another service and more about building a repeatable system for delivering it.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;HubSpot AEO helps agencies build that system by bringing together AI monitoring, content recommendations and creation based on visibility gaps, and reporting in one platform. Agencies can use that infrastructure to build AEO into their existing client workflows instead of managing every engagement from scratch.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Clients are already asking for AEO. The infrastructure to deliver it efficiently is what separates a reactive answer from a scalable practice.&lt;/p&gt;  
&lt;img src="https://track.hubspot.com/__ptq.gif?a=53&amp;amp;k=14&amp;amp;r=https%3A%2F%2Fblog.hubspot.com%2Fmarketing%2Faeo-guide-for-marketing-agencies&amp;amp;bu=https%253A%252F%252Fblog.hubspot.com%252Fmarketing&amp;amp;bvt=rss" alt="" width="1" height="1" style="min-height:1px!important;width:1px!important;border-width:0!important;margin-top:0!important;margin-bottom:0!important;margin-right:0!important;margin-left:0!important;padding-top:0!important;padding-bottom:0!important;padding-right:0!important;padding-left:0!important; "&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Enterprise brand teams face a complex version of AEO that most tools weren’t built for. A single brand might span a dozen product lines, operate in multiple languages, and compete in markets where local answer engines have their own citation patterns.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Get Started with HubSpot's AEO Tool" height="58" width="335" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;When content teams, regional marketers, and product groups handle AEO separately, visibility becomes fragmented. The challenge becomes coordinating AEO across the organization. While individual teams may be able to see how individual product lines or markets are performing, they don’t have a clear picture of how the brand is showing up overall.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Scaling AEO at the enterprise level requires centralized monitoring, cross-team workflows, and the ability to tie visibility investments to revenue outcomes. Let’s get into each.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Monitor brand visibility across products, markets, and answer engines from one place.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;At the enterprise level, brand visibility across answer engines is a matrix, not a single number. Marketing teams need to understand how different product lines are cited, how visibility varies by region, and how the brand is positioned relative to competitors in each market. They also need to track those changes across answer engines.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;When that data lives in disconnected tools or requires manual assembly, enterprise AEO monitoring quickly becomes difficult to scale. Teams end up with snapshots of individual products or markets but no way to see the full picture.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/how%20seo%20works%2c%20example%20of%20results%20from%20hubspot%20aeo.webp?width=650&amp;amp;height=366&amp;amp;name=how%20seo%20works%2c%20example%20of%20results%20from%20hubspot%20aeo.webp" width="650" height="366" alt="Enterprise AEO, HubSpot AEO brand visibility dashboard " style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt;’s Brand Visibility Dashboard consolidates brand visibility score, share of voice, and citations data across a brand’s entire footprint. Enterprise teams can segment visibility by product line or market and track trends across AI engines from one view.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The results speak for themselves: &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt; users generate 2.7x more MQLs, according to HubSpot internal data. This gives teams a way to connect AEO visibility with the broader marketing outcomes they already measure.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;But monitoring visibility is only the first step. Enterprise teams also need a way to coordinate those insights and turn them into action.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Coordinate AEO recommendations across content and regional teams.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Generating AEO recommendations is the easy part. The challenge is getting those recommendations acted on by content teams in multiple regions, working across different languages and editorial calendars.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Recommendations are ineffective when they sit in a dashboard that content teams don’t have access to, or arrive as ad hoc requests without priority or context. This creates a gap between identifying a visibility opportunity and actually acting on it.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/AEO-for-brand-marketing-3-20260919-8343173.webp?width=567&amp;amp;height=306&amp;amp;name=AEO-for-brand-marketing-3-20260919-8343173.webp" width="567" height="306" alt="enterprise AEO, HubSpot AEO recommendation feature " style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 567px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Enterprise AEO requires coordinated action, not just data. &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt; surfaces recommendations based on a company’s current visibility gaps and citation opportunities. Content teams can act on those recommendations within HubSpot, deploying &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/artificial-intelligence/build-demand"&gt;content agent&lt;/a&gt; to help them quickly generate optimized content. This keeps AEO execution connected to the workflows they already use.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Once teams are aligned on acting on AEO insights, one challenge remains: Proving that the investment is driving business results.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Attribute AEO investment to revenue outcomes at the enterprise level.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Enterprise stakeholders don’t want to know how many citations a campaign earned. They want to know how AEO investment is affecting pipeline, MQLs, and market share.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Most enterprise AEO programs fall short when tying AEO to revenue outcomes. Without a clear connection from brand visibility to business outcomes, AEO can be difficult to evaluate as it competes for budget against channels that have established attribution models. The work gets done, but the case for sustained investment is hard to make.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;With &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt; connected to CRM data in &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/marketing"&gt;Marketing Hub&lt;/a&gt; Pro and Enterprise, marketing teams can build custom reporting to see whether increases in share of voice or citations line up with changes in inbound volume, MQL rates, or pipeline.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Scale enterprise AEO with the right infrastructure.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Enterprise AEO requires infrastructure that helps teams monitor AI visibility across products and markets, coordinate content efforts, and connect visibility trends to business outcomes. As AI becomes a larger part of buyer research, centralized processes make it easier to identify gaps and act on opportunities at scale.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;HubSpot AEO can support that process by bringing brand visibility, citation insights, and content recommendations into existing marketing workflows. The goal isn’t just to increase visibility, but to build a repeatable approach for managing AEO and understanding its impact on the business.&lt;/p&gt;  
&lt;img src="https://track.hubspot.com/__ptq.gif?a=53&amp;amp;k=14&amp;amp;r=https%3A%2F%2Fblog.hubspot.com%2Fmarketing%2Faeo-guide-for-enterprise&amp;amp;bu=https%253A%252F%252Fblog.hubspot.com%252Fmarketing&amp;amp;bvt=rss" alt="" width="1" height="1" style="min-height:1px!important;width:1px!important;border-width:0!important;margin-top:0!important;margin-bottom:0!important;margin-right:0!important;margin-left:0!important;padding-top:0!important;padding-bottom:0!important;padding-right:0!important;padding-left:0!important; "&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Buyer behavior has changed since the advent of artificial intelligence. Now, before ever filling out a form or clicking an ad, prospects are likely asking AI for recommendations, comparing vendors, and gathering answers. Those interactions shape which companies make the shortlist, but they often happen outside the systems marketing operations teams use to measure performance.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Get Started with HubSpot's AEO Tool" height="58" width="335" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Buyers asking AI for recommendations creates a new accountability gap. The tools and processes built for search and paid traffic weren’t designed to capture how AI-assisted discovery works.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The question is how to build the infrastructure to connect AEO to the buyer journey and revenue. To make AEO measurable and actionable, marketing operations teams need to connect brand visibility data to their CRM, incorporate AI-driven touchpoints into attribution, and automate ongoing monitoring and reporting.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Integrate AEO performance data into your CRM and marketing reports.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;If AEO signals aren’t connected to the CRM, the attribution model can’t account for an important part of the buyer journey.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Marketing attribution is only as strong as the tracking infrastructure behind it. When a buyer’s first meaningful touchpoint happens inside an answer engine through a citation, a brand mention, or a recommended link, that moment typically falls outside traditional reporting.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;But the more buyers use answer engines to research products, vendors, and solutions, the more the discovery journey happens before a prospect ever reaches a company’s website. In turn, its contact and pipeline data becomes more incomplete.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Consider this example: If 30% of a brand’s inbound traffic now has AI-assisted discovery as a precursor touchpoint, but the attribution model can’t capture those interactions, every revenue report will understate marketing’s influence.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Connecting AEO data to the CRM helps fix the attribution blind spot. &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt; connects visibility signals such as brand visibility score, share of voice across answer engines, and citations to contact and deal records through CRM configuration. Marketers can see which channels are driving AI-sourced traffic and map that data back to pipeline.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;According to HubSpot internal data, teams who use HubSpot AEO create 78% more contacts.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Once AEO data is flowing into the CRM, the next step is building attribution logic that accounts for how AI-driven touchpoints fit into the buyer journey.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Build attribution models that capture AI-driven touchpoints in the buyer journey.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Traditional first-touch and last-touch attribution can miss the influence AI has on buyers before they ever visit a site. Even multi-touch models that rely on click data miss that influence. These models simply weren’t built for a world where a buyer gets brand context from an AI.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;A buyer might ask an answer engine which vendors solve a particular problem, encounter your brand in the answer, and only later visit your website through an organic search, direct visit, or paid campaign. A click-based attribution model may credit the later interaction while missing the AI interaction that helped create awareness in the first place. That makes AEO difficult to evaluate using conventional channel reporting.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;When AEO activity isn’t incorporated into attribution, there is no obvious reason to keep a channel that appears to generate little ROI. The truth is, AEO actually influenced demand earlier in the journey, but the model can’t see it.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/how%20seo%20works%2c%20example%20of%20results%20from%20hubspot%20aeo.webp?width=650&amp;amp;height=366&amp;amp;name=how%20seo%20works%2c%20example%20of%20results%20from%20hubspot%20aeo.webp" width="650" height="366" alt="AEO for marketing operations, HubSpot AEO brand visibility dashboard" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AEO reporting can provide another layer of context. &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt;’s Brand Visibility Dashboard surfaces how a brand is represented in answer engines over time, including share of voice trends and citation growth. Marketing teams can use those trend lines alongside CRM pipeline data to understand how changes in AEO visibility affect downstream movement.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Once AEO is part of the attribution framework, the remaining challenge is keeping the data current without creating a manual reporting burden.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Automate AEO monitoring and reporting so the data stays current.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;AEO needs to become part of the regular reporting cadence, not a quarterly snapshot assembled manually by the operations team. Answer engines update their answers continuously, and a brand’s presence can shift week over week based on content changes, competitor moves, and new publications entering the citation pool.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;One-off reporting becomes especially limiting in the face of constantly changing AI answers. If staying current requires marketers to pull data manually, update spreadsheets, and build reports from scratch, AEO quickly becomes another ad hoc request for the operations team.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/aeo%20trends%2c%20hubspot%20aeo.webp?width=650&amp;amp;height=488&amp;amp;name=aeo%20trends%2c%20hubspot%20aeo.webp" width="650" height="488" alt="AEO for marketing operations, HubSpot AEO share of voice " style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Automation turns AEO into an ongoing signal. &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt; continuously tracks brand visibility score, citations, and share of voice without requiring manual pulls. Ops leaders don’t need to manually pull AEO metrics because visibility score, citations, and share of voice refresh automatically inside the tool.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Measuring AI Influence on Pipeline and Revenue&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;For marketing operations, the opportunity is about building the infrastructure to understand how AI-assisted discovery contributes to the buyer journey, then connecting that activity to the revenue data the business already relies on. As AI becomes a more common starting point for research, teams that can connect visibility signals with contacts, pipeline, and conversion data will have a clearer picture of how buyers discover and evaluate their brand.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;With tools like HubSpot AEO, marketing operations teams can bring AI visibility, citation, and share of voice data into the broader reporting workflow, making it easier to monitor changes and connect them to downstream outcomes. The infrastructure to measure AI’s influence is becoming part of the modern marketing stack; the next step is putting that infrastructure to work.&lt;/p&gt;  
&lt;img src="https://track.hubspo...

&lt;p&gt;Demand generation has been built around the assumption that buyers will come to a brand when they are ready to learn about its category, whether through search, ads, content, or other channels. The funnel starts when a prospect arrives somewhere the business can see, measure, and influence it. But AI is changing what happens before that point.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Get Started with HubSpot's AEO Tool" height="58" width="335" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Increasingly, buyers begin their research inside AI interfaces. They ask a question, get a curated answer, and form opinions about a category before arriving on a vendor website. If your brand isn’t part of the AI-generated answer, you’re not in the conversation that shapes the shortlist.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Demand generation teams that understand the AI shift are extending their funnel. The goal is to expand the traditional funnel to ensure brand presence at this new early stage of buyer research, not replace it altogether.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Demand generation teams need to extend the funnel upstream to generate qualified pipeline as AI reshapes buyer discovery. Teams need to understand where buyers encounter their brand in AI answers, create content that reinforces those research journeys, and connect AEO performance to MQLs and pipeline.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Understand where AI-assisted buyers encounter your brand during research.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Before demand generation teams can capture AI-driven demand, they need to map where their brand appears in AI research and where competitors appear instead of them. Start by charting the AI landscape for your category. Investigate:&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;ul&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Which category-level prompts surface competitors but not your brand?&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Which answer engines are most active for your category and target buyers?&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;What context surrounds your brand when it is cited?&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;Which topics and questions consistently shape vendor recommendations?&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Without this map, demand generation teams risk only optimizing the part of the funnel they can measure while remaining blind to the new phase where buyers now form their opinions. They may have a well-optimized inbound program while missing key research interactions that influence buyers before they become identifiable prospects.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/ai%20search%20strategy%20built%20with%20hubspot%20aeo.webp?width=650&amp;amp;height=366&amp;amp;name=ai%20search%20strategy%20built%20with%20hubspot%20aeo.webp" width="650" height="366" alt="ai search strategy built with hubspot aeo" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt; addresses the potential optimization blind spot. The Brand Visibility Dashboard and citation analysis in HubSpot AEO help marketers see where their brand appears in AI-generated answers, organized by engine, query type, and competitive context. Teams can identify the specific prompts that drive buyers to their category but don’t surface their brand. This reveals exactly where their gaps in AI visibility and demand generation are.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The visibility into how a brand is being cited and the exact prompts driving buyers but not surfacing the brand gives teams a starting point. The next step is turning those gaps into content that helps buyers move from AI-assisted research to active evaluation.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Create content that captures demand from AI-influenced buyer journeys.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Once teams understand their AI visibility gaps, they need to create content designed to capture AI-influenced buyers at the evaluation stage, not content that sends them back to the beginning of the funnel.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Buyers influenced by AI arrive on a website with more context than traditional inbound leads. Since an answer engine has told them that certain vendors are worth evaluating, they need content that is stronger than what typical top-of-funnel leads are looking for.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Treating AI-referred visitors like any other inbound audience can create unnecessary friction. Sending a buyer who has already researched the category to a generic awareness page or introductory ebook forces them to retrace steps they’ve already taken. Instead, demand generation teams should create content that answers the specific questions buyers use to evaluate vendors: how solutions compare, which use cases they support, what differentiates one approach from another, and what evidence supports the claims.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;For example, if a buyer has already decided to evaluate three vendors based on an AI research session, a brand’s content needs to quickly reinforce why it deserves to be considered. Otherwise, competitors who also showed up in the original AI answer and then reinforced it with better content will outstrip you.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/geo-kpis-2-20260423-7543786.webp?width=650&amp;amp;height=366&amp;amp;name=geo-kpis-2-20260423-7543786.webp" width="650" height="366" alt="AEO for demand generation teams, HubSpot AEO recommendations feature " style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt;’s Recommendations identify questions and topics that a content library isn’t adequately addressing to appear in AI search. &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/artificial-intelligence/build-demand"&gt;Content agent&lt;/a&gt; helps demand gen teams fill those gaps quickly, producing structured content that addresses the research questions driving AI-assisted discovery, aligned with how AEO tracks citation-worthy content.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Having the right content for answer engines pays off. According to HubSpot data, businesses that use HubSpot AEO generate 2.7x more marketing qualified leads (MQLs).&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;But content creation alone doesn’t demonstrate business impact. Demand generation teams also need to connect AEO activity to the metrics they already use to manage performance.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Measure AEO’s impact on MQL volume and pipeline.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Demand generation teams are accountable to MQLs, pipeline, and revenue, not to visibility scores. Making AEO a permanent line in the budget requires demonstrating that AI-assisted discovery is moving the numbers.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Measurement and attribution are challenging because AI discovery rarely happens in isolation. Buyers who first encounter a brand in an AI answer often touch multiple channels before converting. Crediting AEO in that path requires more sophisticated modeling than last-click, and most teams don’t have it built yet.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/SEO%20reporting%2c%20HubSpot%20AEO%20tool%20dashboard.webp?width=650&amp;amp;height=366&amp;amp;name=SEO%20reporting%2c%20HubSpot%20AEO%20tool%20dashboard.webp" width="650" height="366" alt="AEO for demand generation teams, HubSpot AEO prompt tracking" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: ...

&lt;p&gt;Product marketing’s core job is positioning: Deciding how a product should be described, what category it competes in, and which differentiators matter most to buyers. The results are deployed through sales, content, and campaigns. But now there’s a channel that interprets and rebroadcasts your positioning at scale without asking permission: answer engines.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a class="cta_button" href="https://www.hubspot.com/cs/ci/?pg=9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18&amp;amp;pid=53&amp;amp;ecid=&amp;amp;hseid=&amp;amp;hsic="&gt;&lt;img class="hs-cta-img " style="height: auto !important; width: auto !important; max-width: 100% !important;border-width: 0px; /*hs-extra-styles*/; margin: 0 auto; display: block; margin-top: 20px; margin-bottom: 20px" alt="Get Started with HubSpot's AEO Tool" height="58" width="335" src="https://no-cache.hubspot.com/cta/default/53/9dd5e54b-fbef-4dd0-bc44-1689feb1ea18.png" align="middle"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;When a buyer asks an AI assistant about your product category, they get a confident summary answer synthesized from hundreds of sources, including reviews, comparisons, competitor content, and industry coverage. If your owned content isn’t in that source mix, your positioning is being written for you by everyone else.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Product marketing teams with strong AEO visibility do three critical things: Actively monitor what answer engines say about their products; create the owned content that shapes those descriptions; and track whether their positioning investments change how AI represents them to buyers.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Monitor how AI answer engines describe and position your product.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Monitoring highlights what you need to reposition and where. It’s easy to spot product positioning drift in traditional channels. You can read competitor ads, check your own landing pages, and listen to sales calls. But it’s harder with AI answers. If an answer engine draws on stale or competitor-influenced product descriptions, buyers may get inaccurate information or positioning about your product, and you may never know unless you have the right signals in place.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hubfs/MH_AEO_Prompts_EN_03102026.png" width="0" height="0" alt="HubSpot AEO brand visibility dashboard" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt;’s Brand Visibility Dashboard lets teams track which prompts surface their brand and what context surrounds those citations. Marketers can monitor how their product is described across answer engines, including mentions, how the brand is framed relative to competitors, and identify specific areas where the AI narrative doesn’t match the intended positioning.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Create authoritative owned content that shapes AI-generated descriptions.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Answer engines synthesize their responses from the sources they consider most authoritative. For product positioning, that means owned content that clearly, specifically, and credibly articulates what your product does, who it’s for, and how it compares in a structured way that’s easy for answer engines to parse and excerpt.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Product marketing teams without a systematic approach to AEO content often publish marketing-heavy pages that aren’t optimized for answer engines extracting factual claims. So answer engines skip over your content and cite competitors who publish more extractable content.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://blog.hubspot.com/hs-fs/hubfs/MH_AEO_Recommendations_EN_03102026.png?width=650&amp;amp;height=366&amp;amp;name=MH_AEO_Recommendations_EN_03102026.png" width="650" height="366" alt="HubSpot AEO Recommendations tool" style="margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; display: block; width: 650px; height: auto; max-width: 100%;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/aeo"&gt;HubSpot AEO&lt;/a&gt;’s Recommendations tool provides specific, actionable content guidance based on your citation and visibility data. The &lt;a href="https://www.hubspot.com/products/artificial-intelligence/build-demand"&gt;content agent&lt;/a&gt; feature helps you build the customized pages and structured content that answer those queries with your positioning front and center, giving answer engines high-quality source material to draw from.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;h2&gt;Track how improvements in AI product visibility affect pipeline quality.&lt;/h2&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;Buyers who come in with accurate expectations close faster, churn less, and require less sales education. Effective AEO can shape buyer expectations before the first touchpoint, so improving product visibility in answer engines should boost both volume and pipeline quality.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;But product marketing’s contribution to pipeline quality is notoriously hard to measure, and AEO is easy to deprioritize if you can’t prove the ROI. To translate visibility scores into a revenue story, you need a measurement framework that connects AI visibility improvements to pipeline metrics.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;HubSpot lets you connect brand visibility data to your CRM. Once teams build the attribution view, marketers can compare pipeline velocity, close rates, and deal quality for buyers who arrived through AI-referred channels. Over time, that gives teams the data to argue that accurate AI positioning is a valuable commercial outcome, not just a visibility metric.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;The proof is in the results: HubSpot research shows AEO customers generate 2.6x more leads.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;For product marketers, positioning has always been shaped by sources you don’t control. What’s changed is the scale and speed at which those sources are synthesized into the first answer buyers see. Product marketing teams that build owned content designed for AI citation can take control of their brand positioning and evolve the narrative to meet customers where they’re at.&lt;/p&gt;  
